## Game Architecture

### Screens

The app has three screens controlled by a `screen` state variable:
- `"setup"` → SetupScreen
- `"faceoff"` → FaceOffScreen
- `"board"` → BoardScreen

### Game Flow (critical — understand before touching game logic)

```
startGame(t1, t2, secs, nr)
  ├── FREE PACK + any user     → commitGame(..., false)   [no tokens spent]
  ├── PREMIUM PACK + signed out → show ConversionModal
  ├── PREMIUM PACK + signed in  → setPendingGame(...)
  │     └── SpendConfirmModal confirms → commitGame(..., true)
  └── PREMIUM PACK + insufficient balance → show SpendConfirmModal (buy-more state)

commitGame(t1, t2, secs, nr, usedTokens)
  ├── Lazy-loads premium pack questions from API when needed
  ├── POST /api/tokens/spend (game_id) if usedTokens === true — server validates balance
  ├── Merges free + premium + custom surveys; shuffles playable question list
  └── setScreen("faceoff")
```

Never bypass `startGame`. Never deduct tokens outside of `commitGame` (and never client-side only — spend must hit the API).
Always pass `usedTokens` as a boolean — never undefined.

### Token Rules

- Default `tokensPerGame` is **2** for Survey Showdown; live value comes from `game_config` via `GET /api/config` (`useProductConfig().surveyShowdownTokensPerGame`)
- Free packs (`is_free: true`) NEVER cost tokens, even for signed-in users
- Premium packs and Random Mix cost `tokensPerGame` tokens
- Playthrough ads on FaceOff and Board are shown only for signed-out users
- Signed-in users do not see playthrough ads once auth is resolved
- Token balance lives on `currentUser.tokenBalance` — always update via `onTokensUpdated`
- Never mutate token balance directly in child components

### currentUser Shape

```ts
{
  id: string
  email: string
  username: string
  tokenBalance: number
  emailVerified: boolean
  referralsClaimed: number  // 0–3
}
```

