## API Conventions

### Namespace rules

- Product-level (shared across all GNG games): `/api/config`, `/api/auth/`, `/api/tokens/`, `/api/tokens/bundles`, `/api/referrals/`, `/api/feedback`
- Game-specific: `/api/survey-showdown/`
- Future games: `/api/word-blitz/`, `/api/trivia-rush/`, etc.
- NEVER put game-specific logic in product-level routes

### Auth

- All protected endpoints require a valid Supabase JWT in the Authorization header
- Validate server-side using Supabase service role key — never trust client-supplied user IDs
- RLS is enabled: users only see their own surveys, history, tokens

### Key endpoint behaviors

- `GET /api/config` — public product policy + per-game `tokensPerGame` from `game_config`
- `POST /api/auth/*` — signup, email verification (Resend + Turnstile where applicable)
- `POST /api/tokens/spend` — validates balance server-side before deducting; requires `game_id`; rejects if insufficient
- `POST /api/tokens/webhook` — Stripe webhook (raw body; registered before JSON parsers)
- `GET /api/survey-showdown/packs` — official pack catalog; premium question bodies via `GET .../packs/:id/questions`
- `GET/POST/PUT/DELETE /api/survey-showdown/custom-surveys` — user surveys and collections (RLS + auth)
- `POST /api/survey-showdown/judge` — checks `judge_cache` first; Claude Haiku on miss; never exposes Anthropic key to frontend
- `POST /api/survey-showdown/history` — requires `game_id: "survey_showdown"` in request body; enforces 50-record rolling window
- `POST /api/feedback` — requires `game_id` for per-game dashboard filtering
- `DELETE /api/survey-showdown/custom-surveys/collections/:id` — deletes collection only; surveys become uncategorized (`collection_id` cleared)

### Zod validation

Every endpoint validates its request body and query params with Zod before any
business logic. Return 400 with a structured error object on validation failure.

