## Database Conventions

### Naming

- Shared tables: `users`, `user_tokens`, `token_bundles`, `purchases`, `referrals`, `feedback`, `game_sessions`, `game_config`, `judge_cache`, `product_policy`, `signup_verification_challenges`
- Survey Showdown tables: **`su_` prefix** — `su_survey_packs`, `su_survey_questions`, `su_survey_answers`, `su_survey_pack_tags`, `su_custom_surveys`, `su_custom_survey_collections`, `su_survey_showdown_sessions`
- All new game tables must use the same game-specific prefix convention (`su_` for Survey Showdown)
- Supabase SQL routines/triggers: canonical source `backend/docs/supabase-public-routines.sql`; follow `backend/docs/database-routines-workflow.md` when editing

### game_sessions table

`game_id` column identifies which game the session belongs to. Survey Showdown
always writes `game_id = "survey_showdown"`. Never query game_sessions without
filtering by game_id unless you intentionally want cross-game data.

### Migrations

- Always use `prisma migrate dev --name <descriptive-name>` for new migrations
- Never edit migration files after they've been applied
- Staging and local share the same Supabase project — run migrations once to cover both
- Production: `npx prisma migrate deploy` against `good-night-games-production`
- When changing `MAX_REFERRALS` in backend env, also update `product_policy.max_referrals` in the database

