## Environment & Mock Mode

### Three environments

| Environment | Supabase Project            | Stripe Keys  | Deploy targets |
|----|----|-----|----------------|
| Local       | good-night-games-staging   | sk_test_...  | localhost:3000 / :3001 |
| Staging     | good-night-games-staging   | sk_test_...  | Vercel preview + Railway staging |
| Production  | good-night-games-production | sk_live_... | Vercel + Railway (alpha releases today) |

**Staging safeguards:** backend `staging-origin-guard` (`FRONTEND_URL`, `ALLOWED_ORIGINS`, `STAGING_ENFORCE_ORIGIN`); optional frontend Basic auth via `STAGING_PASSWORD` in `frontend/src/proxy.ts`.

Key env files: `backend/.env.example`, `frontend/.env.example` (AdSense, Turnstile, Stripe publishable key, `NEXT_PUBLIC_BACKEND_URL`).

### NEXT_PUBLIC_MOCK_MODE

Mock/simulate buttons MUST be gated:

```tsx
const isMockMode = process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_MOCK_MODE === 'true';
{isMockMode && <button onClick={handleSimulate}>🧪 Simulate...</button>}
```

Present in `frontend/.env.local` and staging Vercel. Intentionally absent from
production Vercel builds — Next.js compiles these branches out at build time.

Mock elements that must be gated (complete list):
- "🧪 SIMULATE EMAIL LINK CLICK" (AuthModal — verify state)
- "🧪 SIMULATE EMAIL LINK CLICK" (AuthModal — magic-sent state)
- "MOCK VERIFY" (SetupHeader — email verification banner shortcut)

