## Release Status & Phase Awareness

**Current state (May 2026):** Survey Showdown is **live in production** on Vercel + Railway, shipped through **GitHub alpha pre-releases** (`scripts/prepare-release.ps1` with `-PreRelease alpha`). The first **beta** release is the next milestone; expect ongoing architecture and UX tweaks until then.

| Phase | Status | Deliverable |
|----|-----|----|
| 1–3   | ✅ Done | Original prototype UI (migrated to TypeScript components) |
| 4     | ✅ Done | Backend scaffold + Prisma schema |
| 5     | ✅ Done | Product + Survey Showdown API endpoints |
| 6     | ✅ Done | Next.js App Router + real Supabase auth (`AuthContext`, `/auth/callback`) |
| 7     | ✅ Done | Stripe token bundles + webhook |
| 8     | ✅ Done | AI judge on backend (`judge_cache`, Haiku pipeline) |
| 9     | ✅ Done | Referrals, feedback, history, custom surveys wired |
| 10    | ✅ Done (alpha) | Production deploy (Vercel frontend, Railway API, Supabase production DB) |
| Beta  | ⬜ Next | First public beta release; stabilize APIs and polish |

### Release workflow

- Branch from `develop`; cut releases with `./scripts/prepare-release.sh --bump <patch|minor|major> [--pre-release alpha|beta]` (or the `.ps1` equivalent on Windows)
- Agent guidance: `.cursor/skills/prepare-release/SKILL.md`
- Do not merge release PRs unless explicitly asked

### Guidance for changes during alpha

- **Prefer real API + Supabase paths** — mock-only flows are dev exceptions (`NEXT_PUBLIC_MOCK_MODE`), not the default product path
- **Expect churn** — schema, judge contract, pack loading, and auth edge cases may still change before beta; keep migrations backward-safe and update tests when behavior shifts
- **Do not regress** token spend (`commitGame` → `POST /api/tokens/spend`), JWT validation, RLS, or secret handling for convenience

